{
  "reason": "State duties beside the medical license (2026-11-18). (1) rules:getStateReq and rules:getStateEntry for AL, DE, KY and PA (MD and DO): a one-time topic whose rule counts from licensure gains a `within` object (data only; the compliance engine does not read it, so no engine output for AL, KY or PA moves). AL Ethics (professional boundaries): within 12 months of licensure, dated only after the Dec 31, 2025 deadline for existing licensees (albme.gov licensure-cme-requirement). KY Pediatric Abusive Head Trauma: within 5 years of licensure for the boards KRS 311.601(2)(b) names. PA Organ and Tissue Donation: within 5 years of initial licensure for a license issued on or after May 1, 2026 (49 Pa. Code 16.19(c)(1)(ii); DO 25.271(a)(6)(i)(B)); the PA keys were already reviewed for ticket 53890221 and name that output as previousReviewedHash. DE Delaware Controlled Substance Law: within the first year of a new Delaware CSR (24 Del. Admin. Code UCSA Regs. 3.1.2). (2) engine:DE:* and evidence:DE (MD and DO): the DE Controlled Substances topic note adds that the 2 hours are attested at each CSR renewal (registrations expire June 30 of odd years; dpr.delaware.gov/boards/controlledsubstances/renewal), not at the license renewal, and that the app counts them in the license window. Only that note text moves; every hour, window and met flag is unchanged.",
